From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] virtual: count guest memory by class while the host backs
 some

While the host backs guest memory (the dev donor pool behind 0148), log every 30 s, under virtual_mutex, what the guest's committed memory is made of: each view's committed runs by protection, size and whether the view is only partly committed, inside or outside the 0148 window, image, section and system views, each with its committed size and its footprint (host pages mincore reports in core or compressed, the host-backed ones apart). Also log every guest commit's bytes by what 0148 made of them (backed, refused, under 1 MiB, not RW, write-watched, already partly committed, ...). The warmer's address-space walk then runs every 30 s too and splits each band's dirty pages in shared objects, and its footprint line adds the graphics and purgeable ledgers.

Nothing changes what Wine maps: the commit path still asks the swap tier first and then 0148, as before.

Class: diagnostics
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-14-donor-pool-reuse.md
Offered-upstream: no; optional iOS host experiment
